{"path":"3/library/string.templatelib.html","title":"string.templatelib — Support for template string literals","description":"Source code: Lib/string/templatelib.py","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"module-string.templatelib"},{"type":"anchor","id":"string-templatelib-support-for-template-string-literals"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"string.templatelib"},{"type":"text","value":" — Support for template string literals"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.14/Lib/string/templatelib.py","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lib/string/templatelib.py"}]}]},{"type":"thematic_break"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"seealso","title":"See also","children":[{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#f-strings","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Format strings"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#t-strings","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Template string literal (t-string) syntax"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"index-0"},{"type":"link","href":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0750/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PEP 750"}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"template-strings"},{"type":"anchor","id":"id1"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Template strings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.14."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Template strings are a mechanism for custom string processing. They have the full flexibility of Python’s "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#f-strings","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"f-strings"}]},{"type":"text","value":", but return a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Template","title":"string.templatelib.Template","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instance that gives access to the static and interpolated (in curly brackets) parts of a string "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"before"}]},{"type":"text","value":" they are combined."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To write a t-string, use a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'t'"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix instead of an "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'f'"},{"type":"text","value":", like so:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"pycon","code":">>> pi = 3.14\n>>> t't-strings are new in Python {pi!s}!'\nTemplate(\n   strings=('t-strings are new in Python ', '!'),\n   interpolations=(Interpolation(3.14, 'pi', 's', ''),)\n)"},{"type":"anchor","id":"types"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Template","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"string.templatelib.Template"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":" class describes the contents of a template string. It is immutable, meaning that attributes of a template cannot be reassigned."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The most common way to create a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":" instance is to use the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#t-strings","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"template string literal syntax"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This syntax is identical to that of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#f-strings","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"f-strings"}]},{"type":"text","value":", except that it uses a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"t"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix in place of an "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"f"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> cheese = 'Red Leicester'\n>>> template = t\"We're fresh out of {cheese}, sir.\"\n>>> type(template)\n<class 'string.templatelib.Template'>"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Templates are stored as sequences of literal "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Template.strings","title":"string.templatelib.Template.strings","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"strings"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and dynamic "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Template.interpolations","title":"string.templatelib.Template.interpolations","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"interpolations"}]},{"type":"text","value":". A "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Template.values","title":"string.templatelib.Template.values","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"values"}]},{"type":"text","value":" attribute holds the values of the interpolations:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> template = t'Ah! We do have {cheese}.'\n>>> template.strings\n('Ah! We do have ', '.')\n>>> template.interpolations\n(Interpolation('Camembert', ...),)\n>>> template.values\n('Camembert',)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"strings"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple has one more element than "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"interpolations"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"values"},{"type":"text","value":"; the interpolations “belong” between the strings. This may be easier to understand when tuples are aligned"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"template.strings:  ('Ah! We do have ',              '.')\ntemplate.values:   (                   'Camembert',    )"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attributes"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Template.strings","term":[{"type":"text","value":"strings"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#tuple","title":"tuple","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tuple"}]},{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#str","title":"str","children":[{"type":"text","value":"str"}]},{"type":"text","value":","},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"..."},{"type":"text","value":"]"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#tuple","title":"tuple","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"tuple"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of the static strings in the template."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> template = t'Ah! We do have {cheese}.'\n>>> template.strings\n('Ah! We do have ', '.')"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty strings "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"are"}]},{"type":"text","value":" included in the tuple:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> response = 'We do have '\n>>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> template = t'Ah! {response}{cheese}.'\n>>> template.strings\n('Ah! ', '', '.')"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"strings"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple is never empty, and always contains one more string than the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"interpolations"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" tuples:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> t''.strings\n('',)\n>>> t''.values\n()\n>>> t'{'cheese'}'.strings\n('', '')\n>>> t'{'cheese'}'.values\n('cheese',)"}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Template.interpolations","term":[{"type":"text","value":"interpolations"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#tuple","title":"tuple","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tuple"}]},{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Interpolation","title":"string.templatelib.Interpolation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interpolation"}]},{"type":"text","value":","},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"..."},{"type":"text","value":"]"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#tuple","title":"tuple","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"tuple"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of the interpolations in the template."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> template = t'Ah! We do have {cheese}.'\n>>> template.interpolations\n(Interpolation('Camembert', 'cheese', None, ''),)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"interpolations"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple may be empty and always contains one fewer values than the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"strings"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> t'Red Leicester'.interpolations\n()"}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Template.values","term":[{"type":"text","value":"values"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#tuple","title":"tuple","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tuple"}]},{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#object","title":"object","children":[{"type":"text","value":"object"}]},{"type":"text","value":","},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"..."},{"type":"text","value":"]"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tuple of all interpolated values in the template."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> template = t'Ah! We do have {cheese}.'\n>>> template.values\n('Camembert',)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple always has the same length as the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"interpolations"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple. It is always equivalent to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"tuple(i.value for i in template.interpolations)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methods"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Template.__new__","term":[{"type":"text","value":"__new__("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"*"},{"type":"text","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#str","title":"str","children":[{"type":"text","value":"str"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"|"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Interpolation","title":"string.templatelib.Interpolation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interpolation"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While literal syntax is the most common way to create a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":", it is also possible to create them directly using the constructor:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> from string.templatelib import Interpolation, Template\n>>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> template = Template(\n...     'Ah! We do have ', Interpolation(cheese, 'cheese'), '.'\n... )\n>>> list(template)\n['Ah! We do have ', Interpolation('Camembert', 'cheese', None, ''), '.']"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If multiple strings are passed consecutively, they will be concatenated into a single value in the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Template.strings","title":"string.templatelib.Template.strings","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"strings"}]},{"type":"text","value":" attribute. For example, the following code creates a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":" with a single final string:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> from string.templatelib import Template\n>>> template = Template('Ah! We do have ', 'Camembert', '.')\n>>> template.strings\n('Ah! We do have Camembert.',)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If multiple interpolations are passed consecutively, they will be treated as separate interpolations and an empty string will be inserted between them. For example, the following code creates a template with empty placeholders in the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Template.strings","title":"string.templatelib.Template.strings","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"strings"}]},{"type":"text","value":" attribute:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> from string.templatelib import Interpolation, Template\n>>> template = Template(\n...     Interpolation('Camembert', 'cheese'),\n...     Interpolation('.', 'punctuation'),\n... )\n>>> template.strings\n('', '', '')"}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"text","value":"iter(template)"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Iterate over the template, yielding each non-empty string and "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.Interpolation","title":"string.templatelib.Interpolation","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Interpolation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in the correct order:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> list(t'Ah! We do have {cheese}.')\n['Ah! We do have ', Interpolation('Camembert', 'cheese', None, ''), '.']"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"caution","title":"Caution","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty strings are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" included in the iteration:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> response = 'We do have '\n>>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> list(t'Ah! {response}{cheese}.')\n['Ah! ',\n Interpolation('We do have ', 'response', None, ''),\n Interpolation('Camembert', 'cheese', None, ''),\n '.']"}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"text","value":"template + other"}],"definition":[]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"text","value":"template += other"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Concatenate this template with another, returning a new "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":" instance:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> list(t'Ah! ' + t'We do have {cheese}.')\n['Ah! We do have ', Interpolation('Camembert', 'cheese', None, ''), '.']"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Concatenating a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":" and a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"str"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" supported. This is because it is unclear whether the string should be treated as a static string or an interpolation. If you want to concatenate a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":" with a string, you should either wrap the string directly in a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":" (to treat it as a static string) or use an "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Interpolation"},{"type":"text","value":" (to treat it as dynamic):"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> from string.templatelib import Interpolation, Template\n>>> template = t'Ah! '\n>>> # Treat 'We do have ' as a static string\n>>> template += Template('We do have ')\n>>> # Treat cheese as an interpolation\n>>> cheese = 'Camembert'\n>>> template += Template(Interpolation(cheese, 'cheese'))\n>>> list(template)\n['Ah! We do have ', Interpolation('Camembert', 'cheese', None, '')]"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Interpolation","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"string.templatelib.Interpolation"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Interpolation"},{"type":"text","value":" type represents an expression inside a template string. It is immutable, meaning that attributes of an interpolation cannot be reassigned."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interpolations support pattern matching, allowing you to match against their attributes with the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#match","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"match statement"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> from string.templatelib import Interpolation\n>>> interpolation = t'{1. + 2.:.2f}'.interpolations[0]\n>>> interpolation\nInterpolation(3.0, '1. + 2.', None, '.2f')\n>>> match interpolation:\n...     case Interpolation(value, expression, conversion, format_spec):\n...         print(value, expression, conversion, format_spec, sep=' | ')\n...\n3.0 | 1. + 2. | None | .2f"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interpolations are "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#generics","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"generic"}]},{"type":"text","value":" over the types of their values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attributes"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Interpolation.value","term":[{"type":"text","value":"value"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#object","title":"object","children":[{"type":"text","value":"object"}]}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The evaluated value of the interpolation."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> t'{1 + 2}'.interpolations[0].value\n3"}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Interpolation.expression","term":[{"type":"text","value":"expression"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#str","title":"str","children":[{"type":"text","value":"str"}]}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For interpolations created by t-string literals, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"expression"},{"type":"text","value":" is the expression text found inside the curly brackets ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"{"},{"type":"text","value":" & "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"}"},{"type":"text","value":"), including any whitespace, excluding the curly brackets themselves, and ending before the first "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"!"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":":"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"="},{"type":"text","value":" if any is present. For manually created interpolations, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"expression"},{"type":"text","value":" is the arbitrary string provided when constructing the interpolation instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We recommend using valid Python expressions or the empty string for the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"expression"},{"type":"text","value":" field of manually created "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Interpolation"},{"type":"text","value":" instances, although this is not enforced at runtime."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> t'{1 + 2}'.interpolations[0].expression\n'1 + 2'"}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Interpolation.conversion","term":[{"type":"text","value":"conversion"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Literal","title":"typing.Literal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Literal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"text","value":"'a'"},{"type":"text","value":","},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"'r'"},{"type":"text","value":","},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"'s'"},{"type":"text","value":"]"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"|"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/constants.html#None","title":"None","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The conversion to apply to the value, or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"conversion"},{"type":"text","value":" is the optional conversion to apply to the value:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> t'{1 + 2!a}'.interpolations[0].conversion\n'a'"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unlike f-strings, where conversions are applied automatically, the expected behavior with t-strings is that code that "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"processes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Template"},{"type":"text","value":" will decide how to interpret and whether to apply the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"conversion"},{"type":"text","value":". For convenience, the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.templatelib.html#string.templatelib.convert","title":"string.templatelib.convert","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"convert()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function can be used to mimic f-string conversion semantics."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Interpolation.format_spec","term":[{"type":"text","value":"format_spec"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#str","title":"str","children":[{"type":"text","value":"str"}]}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The format specification to apply to the value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"format_spec"},{"type":"text","value":" is an optional, arbitrary string used as the format specification to present the value:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> t'{1 + 2:.2f}'.interpolations[0].format_spec\n'.2f'"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unlike f-strings, where format specifications are applied automatically via the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#format","title":"format","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"format()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" protocol, the expected behavior with t-strings is that code that "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"processes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the interpolation will decide how to interpret and whether to apply the format specification. As a result, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"format_spec"},{"type":"text","value":" values in interpolations can be arbitrary strings, including those that do not conform to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"format()"},{"type":"text","value":" protocol."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methods"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"string.templatelib.Interpolation.__new__","term":[{"type":"text","value":"__new__("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#object","title":"object","children":[{"type":"text","value":"object"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"expression"},{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#str","title":"str","children":[{"type":"text","value":"str"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"conversion"},{"type":"text","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Literal","title":"typing.Literal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Literal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"text","value":"'a'"},{"type":"text","value":","},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"'r'"},{"type":"text","value":","},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"'s'"},{"type":"text","value":"]"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","va